Here's a complete example:

**XAML (ItemsPage.xaml)**

```xml
<ContentPage xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
             x:Class="MyApp.Views.ItemsPage">

    <RefreshView Command="{Binding RefreshCommand}"
                 IsRefreshing="{Binding IsRefreshing}">

        <CollectionView ItemsSource="{Binding Items}"
                        SelectionMode="Single"
                        SelectedItem="{Binding SelectedItem}"
                        SelectionChangedCommand="{Binding ItemSelectedCommand}">
            <CollectionView.ItemTemplate>
                <DataTemplate>
                    <Grid Padding="10">
                        <Label Text="{Binding Name}" FontSize="16" />
                    </Grid>
                </DataTemplate>
            </CollectionView.ItemTemplate>
        </CollectionView>

    </RefreshView>
</ContentPage>
```

**ViewModel bindings explained:**

| Binding | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `Items` | `ObservableCollection<T>` driving the list |
| `IsRefreshing` | `bool` property — set `false` when refresh completes |
| `RefreshCommand` | `IAsyncRelayCommand` that calls your API and repopulates `Items` |
| `SelectedItem` | The currently selected model object (two-way) |
| `ItemSelectedCommand` | Fires on selection change; navigates then nulls `SelectedItem` |

**ViewModel sketch (using CommunityToolkit.Mvvm)**

```csharp
public partial class ItemsViewModel : ObservableObject
{
    private readonly IApiService _api;
    private readonly INavigationService _nav;

    [ObservableProperty] private bool isRefreshing;
    [ObservableProperty] private MyItem? selectedItem;

    public ObservableCollection<MyItem> Items { get; } = new();

    [RelayCommand]
    private async Task RefreshAsync()
    {
        var data = await _api.GetItemsAsync();
        Items.Clear();
        foreach (var item in data) Items.Add(item);
        IsRefreshing = false;
    }

    [RelayCommand]
    private async Task ItemSelectedAsync()
    {
        if (SelectedItem is null) return;
        await _nav.GoToAsync("DetailPage", SelectedItem.Id);
        SelectedItem = null; // reset so user can re-select
    }
}
```

**Key points:**

- Wrapping `CollectionView` in `RefreshView` gives pull-to-refresh; the `IsRefreshing` binding controls the spinner.
- Setting `SelectedItem = null` after navigation allows the same item to be tapped again later.
- `SelectionMode="Single"` ensures only one item highlights at a time.
- Use `Shell.Current.GoToAsync` (or an abstraction) for navigation with query parameters.
